  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Bring a medium saucepan of salted water to the boil for the pasta. Trim the zucchini, quarter lengthwise, then cut into 1cm chunks. Halve the cherry tomatoes. Crush or finely chop 1 garlic clove.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/156828/photos/large/DNY_Recipe_Card_New_Illustration_01-3c5e09c19014ea60abcdf05ac61091d4.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Toast walnuts: Put the walnuts in a cold large frypan over medium heat (see Kitchen 101). Toast, tossing, for 3-4 mins until evenly golden. Remove the walnuts from the pan, reserving the pan.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/156829/photos/large/DNY_Recipe_Card_New_Illustration_02-2926580d9bbc8c56d65fa9aea6b809f9.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook pasta: Cook three-quarters of the pasta in the pan of boiling water for 8-10 mins until al dente. Reserve 2 tbs cooking water, then drain the pasta.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/156830/photos/large/DNY_Recipe_Card_New_Illustration_03-a49ec27f5bf99ddf4ba0511d16af9859.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook vegetables: Meanwhile, heat 2 tbs olive oil in the reserved pan over medium-high heat. Cook the zucchini, stirring, for 3-4 mins until light golden. Add the garlic, tomato, 1 tsp Italian herbs and 2 tsp balsamic vinegar and cook, stirring, for 3-4 mins until softened. Add the spinach leaves and reserved cooking water and cook for 2-3 mins until the spinach is wilted.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/156831/photos/large/DNY_Recipe_Card_New_Illustration_04-bc759d4f4e2c78354fd94ba1a59b85a9.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Meanwhile, finely grate the parmesan. Coarsely chop the walnuts. Add the pasta and half the grated parmesan to the vegetable mixture, stir to combine and season with salt and pepper. Divide the Mediterranean pasta among bowls, scatter over the walnuts and remaining grated parmesan and enjoy.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/156832/photos/large/DNY_Recipe_Card_New_Illustration_05-5a7a1690f603c65ff6737795493d279d.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kitchen 101: Starting with a cold pan ensures the nuts toast evenly and prevents them burning.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/156833/photos/large/DNY_Recipe_Card_New_Illustration_HACK-4d24763fbe97269c0089cc30f420a7fa.jpg"
    }
  ]
